 the assembly that holds the application's code, so whoever can change its bytes can change that code too, and the Runic.Assets build verified it when it packed or embedded it (",{"c":"RunicAssetsDist"},", ",{"c":"RunicAssetsEmbeddedArchive"},"). An asset whose inflated length differs from its declared length, or whose ZIP entry is damaged, fails to open with ",{"see":"T:System.IO.InvalidDataException"},"."]}," ",{"p":[{"see":"M:Runic.Assets.AssetArchiveSource.ValidateAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)"}," checks every asset against its digest on demand, for a resource that another build step embedded. ",{"see":"M:Runic.Assets.AssetArchive.Read(System.IO.Stream,Runic.Assets.AssetArchiveReadOptions)"}," and ",{"see":"M:Runic.Assets.AssetArchive.ReadAsync(System.IO.Stream,Runic.Assets.AssetArchiveReadOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)"},", which read an archive from outside the assembly such as a file, check every digest before they return."]}],"returns":["The source, which reads its assets from the resource."],"params":[{"name":"assembly","doc":["The assembly that holds the resource."]},{"name":"resourceName","doc":["The manifest resource name; ",{"see":"F:Runic.Assets.AssetArchive.DefaultResourceName"}," by default."]},{"name":"options","doc":["The limits; ",{"c":"null"}," uses the defaults."]}],"exceptions":[{"cref":"T:System.ArgumentException","doc":["The assembly has no such resource."]},{"cref":"T:System.IO.InvalidDataException","doc":["The manifest or the ZIP directory is invalid or exceeds a limit of ",{"c":"options"},"."]}]}},{"id":"M:Runic.Assets.AssetArchive.WriteAsync(Runic.Assets.IAssetSource,System.IO.Stream,System.Threading.CancellationToken)","kind":"method","name":"WriteAsync","signature":["public static ",["ValueTask","T:System.Threading.Tasks.ValueTask"]," WriteAsync(",["IAssetSource","T:Runic.Assets.IAssetSource"]," source, ",["Stream","T:System.IO.Stream"]," destination, ",["CancellationToken","T:System.Threading.CancellationToken"